## 4. Conclusion
In summary, we have fabricated the stable core–shell-liked nano­ structure with the Sb nanoparticles encapsulated in the carbon matrix and $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ hollow nanotubes by ingenious $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ coating and galvanic replacement methods. The synthesized Sb⊂CTHNs maintained the ad­ vantages of intrinsic porosity, high specific surface area and stable hollow structure from Fe-MOFs template, presented excellent electro­ chemical performances for Li/Na-ion battery anode. The internal void space, $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ and carbon matrix buffer in Sb⊂CTHNs as insertion/ extraction reaction type layer could hold the volume expansion of Sb nanoparticle unites which could preserve the nanostructure integrity of Sb⊂CTHNs and the formative SEI layer. For Li-ion half cells, the Sb⊂CTHNs anode displayed long cycle stability (demonstrated a reversible capacity of $336.6\ \mathrm{mA}\mathrm{~h~g~}^{-1}$ at the high current density of $2000\mathrm{mAg}^{-1}$ after 1600 cycles) and an admirable rate capability (a high capacity of $434.8\mathrm{mA}$ h ${\bf g}^{-1}$ at $5000\mathrm{mAg}^{-1})$ . For Sb⊂CTHNs//LiMn2O4 full cells, the storage device exhibited stable charge/discharge plateaus of $3.1/3.3\mathrm{V}$ and a reversible capacity of $398.3\mathrm{mA}$ h ${\bf g}^{-1}$ at $100\mathrm{mAg}^{-1}$ after 100 cycles. Such stable cycle performance and superior rate capability (stable capacities of 604.9, 558, 533.4, 516.6, 498.7, 469.9, 347.1 and $558.4~\mathrm{mA}$ h ${\bf g}^{-1}$ at 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, $5000~\mathrm{{mA}}$ ${\bf g}^{-1}$ and back to $100\mathrm{\mA}\mathrm{\g}^{-1}$ , respectively) were also presented of Sb⊂CTHNs as SIBs anode. And the $\mathrm{SbcCTHNs}//\mathrm{Na_{3}V_{2}(P O_{4})_{3}}$ full cells also delivered an outstanding reversible capacity of $497.7\mathrm{mA}$ h ${\bf g}^{-1}$ after 100 cycles with high Coulombic efficiency of $98.0\%$ , excellent rate capability and stable charge/discharge plateaus even at high rate. The current hybridization with $\mathrm{TiO}_{2}$ coating and nanoconfined galvanic replacement approach could contributed for the precursor with crackly structure, high surface area and unique intrinsic porosity, which can construct more stable nanostructure and develop the advantages of precursors, so that extend their promising application in energy, mole­ cule separation and catalysis-related fields.
